</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.6pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 141.74 1.49 C 141.74 23.93 94.49 11.5 94.49 33.94"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 23.62 1.49 C 23.62 19.91 70.87 19.91 70.87 1.49"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 47.25 33.94 C 47.25 3.46 118.11 31.97 118.11 1.49"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 70.87 33.94 C 70.87 18.23 47.25 17.2 47.25 1.49"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 118.11 33.94 C 118.11 18.23 94.49 17.2 94.49 1.49"></path></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For any parameter <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-vector space spanned by all <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math>-Brauer diagrams. We define a composition map</p>
<table id="S3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(n,m)\otimes\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(m,k)\to\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(n,k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝔅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(n,m)\otimes\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(m,k)\to\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which is defined on basis elements as follows: to compose an <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math>-Brauer diagram and an <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,k)</annotation></semantics></math>-Brauer diagram, connect the strands on the bottom of the first diagram with those on the top of the second diagram, erase any loops that are formed in the process, and multiply the result by <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> to the power of the number of erased loops. The following example illustrates a composition <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(5,7)\otimes\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(7,3)\to\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(5,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝔅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(5,7)\otimes\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(7,3)\to\mathfrak{Br}^{(\delta)}(5,3)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
