</table>
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Each entry in this diagram is a twisted commutative algebra, and the arrows in this diagram are morphisms of twisted commutative algebras.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let us remind the reader of the definitions needed to make sense of Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 8.4. ‣ 8. Twisted commutative algebras and tautological rings ‣ Tautological classes with twisted coefficients" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.4</span></a>. <math id="S8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}^{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>∙</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}^{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math> was defined in Definition <a href="#S5.Thmthm2" title="Definition 5.2. ‣ 5. The Künneth decomposition of the tautological ring ‣ Tautological classes with twisted coefficients" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>; it is the graded polynomial algebra on classes <math id="S8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, modulo the geometrically obvious relations of Eq. (<a href="#S5.E5" title="In 5. The Künneth decomposition of the tautological ring ‣ Tautological classes with twisted coefficients" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The maps <math id="S8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(C_{g}^{n})\to\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(C_{g}^{n})\to\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})</annotation></semantics></math> are given by the projectors <math id="S8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}^{\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}^{\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The same is true for the maps <math id="S8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\bullet}(C_{g}^{n})\to R^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\bullet}(C_{g}^{n})\to R^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The maps <math id="S8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})\to\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})\to\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})</annotation></semantics></math> and the twisted commutative algebra structure on <math id="S8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{n\geq 0}\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{n\geq 0}\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})</annotation></semantics></math> are both defined by the fact that <math id="S8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math> is in a canonical way a direct summand of <math id="S8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n}</annotation></semantics></math>. As such, the natural projection <math id="S8.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n}\to\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n}\to\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math> defines the map <math id="S8.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})\to\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\otimes n})\to\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})</annotation></semantics></math>. The multiplication in the twisted commutative algebra <math id="S8.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigoplus_{n\geq 0}\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>CH</mi><mo>∙</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{n\geq 0}\mathrm{CH}^{\bullet}(M_{g},\mathbf{V}^{\langle n\rangle})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by using the composition</p>
<table id="S8.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
